[cot:thought] The axis tick formatter converts values to compact strings like `$15k`, but the audit parser uses a simple numeric parser that does not scale by thousands.
[cot:thought] This mismatch will break axis value validation. The axis maximum is
[cot:thought] 15 while the tooltip reads 14900. The audit parser uses its own inline `parseNum` that ignores the K suffix, even though `parseAxisNumber` supports it. The region edge Y-axis needs a unified formatter so ticks and tooltips match.
[cot:thought] The region-edge Y-axis
[cot:thought] should drop the `fmtK` abbreviation entirely. Tick labels and tooltips will both use the same compact form, such as `15k` and `$15k`.
[cot:thought] This avoids the parser mismatch where the axis reads 15 while the tooltip shows 14900.
[cot:thought] The region-edge tooltip
[cot:thought] should also switch to the compact `k` format. Both the axis tick label and the tooltip will read `$15k`, so the auditor sees 15 for both. This aligns the axis range [0, 16] with the tooltip value 15.
